       "id": "sell-to-afford-the-raid",
       "source": "hand-built",
       "why": "The same shape one move deeper: there is no \u20ac$ ready, so the Gear has to be paid for by selling the other card in hand first. Selling is worth +0.2 to the frozen evaluation and the Gear +2.8, against roughly +48 for attacking, so the greedy order is attack, then sell, then hold a Gear nothing can carry. Two low-impact moves have to come first. Built like a real mid-game board \u2014 three Legends and a real remaining deck a side \u2014 so a value head reading list size, undrawn fraction and Legend RAM is not extrapolating on it.",
